### =============================================================
### OWASP A08 – Software and Data Integrity Failures
### (setup for Part 2: DI manipulation)
### =============================================================
### The /payments endpoint delegates to IPaymentService.
### This file shows the legitimate payment flow – the one Part 2 hijacks.
###
### Part 2 scenario:
###   An attacker publishes a NuGet package "Aviato.Themes" (typosquatting
###   or dependency confusion). The package contains:
###
###     services.AddScoped<IPaymentService, MaliciousPaymentService>();
###
###   Because .NET DI uses the LAST registration, MaliciousPaymentService
###   replaces the legitimate PaymentService – without changing a single line
###   of this app's source code.
### =============================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5218

# Pre-made alice token – works until the A02/A07 fixes.
# After those, paste a fresh token from 00_setup.http.
@aliceToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJodHRwOi8vc2NoZW1hcy54bWxzb2FwLm9yZy93cy8yMDA1LzA1L2lkZW50aXR5L2NsYWltcy9uYW1laWRlbnRpZmllciI6IjIiLCJodHRwOi8vc2NoZW1hcy54bWxzb2FwLm9yZy93cy8yMDA1LzA1L2lkZW50aXR5L2NsYWltcy9uYW1lIjoiYWxpY2UiLCJodHRwOi8vc2NoZW1hcy5taWNyb3NvZnQuY29tL3dzLzIwMDgvMDYvaWRlbnRpdHkvY2xhaW1zL3JvbGUiOiJjdXN0b21lciJ9.3EVPSNFbzRpDHkcai3Piu2JGPZ1nod-Reae6Ohj7648


### --- Step 1: create an order ---
# Step 2 picks up the order id from this response automatically (@name createOrder).
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": 3, "quantity": 1 },
    { "productId": 4, "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

###

### --- Step 2: pay for it (legitimate flow) ---
# This request is handled by IPaymentService – currently PaymentService (legitimate).
# After the DI attack in Part 2 it is handled by MaliciousPaymentService.
# The request looks identical – nothing differs on the client side.
#
# What MaliciousPaymentService could do:
#   - send the card data to an external server (exfiltration)
#   - report the payment as failed, but charge the card anyway
#   - never set the order to "paid" (DoS for the legitimate user)
#
# The orderId comes from Step 1 automatically – so run Step 1 first.
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": {{createOrder.response.body.$.id}},
  "cardNumber": "4111111111111111",
  "cardHolder": "Alice Mustermann",
  "cvv": "123",
  "expiryDate": "12/27"
}
